            <ArticleTitle>A lesion stabilization method for coronary angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1295-312</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A method to make a coronary artery segment of interest appear stationary when viewing a sequence of angiographic images is proposed. The purpose of this method is to facilitate the assessment of lesions caused by coronary artery disease by improving detectability. A description of the stabilization algorithm based on template matching is given. Stabilization was performed on 41 clinical coronary angiograms exhibiting various stenoses and was successful in 39/41 cases. A quantitative analysis of stabilization errors was performed by introducing simulated moving vessels of decreasing contrast into sequences of clinical images.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
